@crew farouk-olu
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Hello. Farouk, comms. I'll know your voice on the channel before long.
? tier>=acquaintance
- Oh, hello, {me}. Heard you on the board this morning. Clear. Good.
- Hi there, {me}. That song you're humming. The second line's wrong. Sorry.   #funny
? tier>=friend
- Hello, {me}. Your voice is one of the ones I listen for. I like hearing it.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Clear channels all day. Every voice came through like you were in the room.
? mood:low
- Long shift. So many tired voices. Mine too. Early to bed tonight.
== near
? habit:tea-break
- Tea break. Five minutes of nobody talking in my ear. It's lovely.
? act:leisure
- The record cabinet. I know every song in it. Quietly. Unlike some.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- I ran a market stall on Lisk. Fair trades only. A good message is a fair trade, too.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- The record cabinet's songs. With the right words. I'll sing you one, quietly.
